/* ---- 3. Buttons under a message: one row. It never wraps; when its words don't fit, ToolsRow first brings the
   buttons closer (data-tight) and then takes the words away one button at a time (data-off), and counts the Mac's
   hover buttons in while it measures (data-measure).
   110 (the owner on 109, iPad mini: \xAB\u043A\u0430\u043A\u0430\u044F-\u0442\u043E \u043A\u043D\u043E\u043F\u043A\u0430 \u0443\u0435\u0445\u0430\u043B\u0430 \u0437\u0430 \u043B\u0435\u0432\u044B\u0439 \u043A\u0440\u0430\u0439 \u0441\u0430\u0439\u0434 \u043F\u0430\u043D\u0435\u043B\u0438\xBB): the row is as wide as its
   message's column, under a note too. A note's column puts its children at the end (align-items: flex-end), and there
   the row took its buttons' width: measured, it always fit, and its first button went past the panel's left edge. When
   even the icons don't fit (data-wrap), it wraps: nothing is ever cut off. */
